hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1557","Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Ash’ath told us, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Zubaid, my father told us, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to the side of the row and straighten the chests of people. The people and their positions, and He says: “Do not differ lest your hearts differ. Indeed, God and His angels pray in the first rows.”"
